---
title: Spaghetti carbonara
servings: 4
tags: [italian, pork, quick, weeknight]
cuisine: italian
time: 25 minutes
source: Spaghetti Carbonara by GialloZafferano, https://giallozafferano.com/recipes/Spaghetti-Carbonara-Bacon-and-egg-spaghetti.html
---

Put a #large pot{} of salted water on to boil.

Cut the rind off the @guanciale{150%g} and cut it into strips about 1 cm thick.

Brown the guanciale in a #nonstick skillet{} over medium-high heat
~{10%minutes}, until crisp but not burnt.

Cook the @dried pasta{320%g}(spaghetti) until al dente.

Whisk the @egg yolks{6}, @Pecorino Romano{50%g}(finely grated) and plenty of
@black pepper{} in a #bowl{} until smooth.

Turn off the heat under the skillet. Lift the guanciale out with a slotted
spoon, leaving the fat behind, and add a ladle of the pasta water to the fat.

Drain the spaghetti straight into the skillet and toss, off the heat. Quickly
stir in the egg mixture until creamy, adding a little more pasta water if it is
tight.

Stir in the guanciale and serve at once, with more @Pecorino Romano{} and pepper
on top.

> Keep the pan off the heat when the eggs go in, or they scramble. The pasta's
> own heat is enough to thicken them.
